  "tree_id": 1361,
  "family": "Arecaceae",
  "memo": "&lt;em&gt;Syagrus romanzoffiana &lt;/em&gt;is a subtropical to tropical feather palm native to the woodlands of South America. Its elegant, arching, and dark green crown is supported by a slender and gray trunk. Bright orange drupes are produced in abundance, enjoyed by birds and small mammals. With its tolerance of light frost, drought, and heat, this is one of the hardiest tropical palms. Its fallen fruits can make a mess of the ground. Otherwise, this fast-grower has become very popular in cultivation.",
