  "california_native": 0,
  "ethnobotanical_info": "The fruits of the Queen Palm are edible and processed into wines or syrups. Its young apical buds are also edible, but their removal kills the tree. Its leaves are a source of fiber for baskets and hats, while its salt-resistant trunks are used for water pipes and construction.&nbsp;&nbsp;",
